tw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240693943?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gts360","html_url":"https://github.com/gts360","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gts360/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gts360/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gts360/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gts360/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gts360/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gts360/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gts360/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gts360/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gts360/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/gts360/django-mcp-server","description":"Django MCP Server is a Django extensions to easily enable AI Agents to interact with Django Apps through the Model Context Protocol it works equally well on WSGI and ASGI","fork":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/collaborators{/collaborator}","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/teams","hooks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/hooks","issue_events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/issues/events{/number}","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/events","assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/assignees{/user}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/branches{/branch}","tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/tags","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/git/blobs{/sha}","git_tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/git/tags{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/deployments","created_at":"2025-05-10T13:14:41Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T17:12:50Z","pushed_at":"2026-03-10T10:38:28Z","git_url":"git://github.com/gts360/django-mcp-server.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:gts360/django-mcp-server.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/gts360/django-mcp-server.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/gts360/django-mcp-server","homepage":"","size":187,"stargazers_count":387,"watchers_count":387,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":59,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":20,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["agentic-ai","ai","django","modelcontextprotocol"],"visibility":"public","forks":59,"open_issues":20,"watchers":387,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### Summary\n\nThe tool's own description promises \"a subset of MongoDB aggregation pipeline JSON\", so a model supplies MongoDB's spelling — and one documented form of $count is then rejected. The complaint is that the package doesn't match the language it advertises.\n\nThe `$group` stage accepts `{\"$count\": 1}` but rejects `{\"$count\": {}}`, which is\nthe form MongoDB itself defines for the `$count` accumulator (MongoDB 5.0+).\nSince the tool description tells the model it is using \"a subset of MongoDB\naggregation pipeline JSON\", a model reaches for the MongoDB spelling first, gets\nan error, and has to retry.\n\n### Reproduce\n\n```json\n{\n  \"collection\": \"listing\",\n  \"search_pipeline\": [\n    {\"$group\": {\"_id\": null, \"n\": {\"$count\": {}}}}\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nResult:\n\n```\nError executing tool query_data_collections:\n$count only supports value 1 or a field reference.\n```\n\nThe same query with `{\"$count\": 1}` succeeds.\n\n### Cause\n\n`mcp_server/query_tool.py`, in the `$group` branch:\n\n```python\nelif op == \"$count\":\n    if arg == 1:\n        annotations[key] = Count(\"id\")\n    elif isinstance(arg, str) and arg.startswith(\"$\"):\n        annotations[key] = Count(_translate_field(arg[1:], lookup_alias_map))\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(\"$count only supports value 1 or a field reference.\")\n```\n\n`{}` is not among the accepted forms.\n\n### Suggested fix\n\nAccept the empty document as equivalent to `1`:\n\n```python\nelif op == \"$count\":\n    if arg == 1 or arg == {}:\n        annotations[key] = Count(\"id\")\n```\n\nThat keeps the existing spellings working and adds the one MongoDB documents.\n(If #65 / #68 land first, this branch becomes `Count(\"pk\")` — the change is the\nsame either way.)\n\n### Why it matters\n\nThis is not a broken tool — the error is a well-formed tool execution error and\na model does self-correct from it, which is what the MCP spec intends. But it\ncosts a round trip on the first aggregation of every session, for a syntax the\ntool's own description implies is supported. Working around it downstream means\ndocumenting the deviation in server instructions, which every deployment then\nhas to carry.\n\n### Environment\n\n- django-mcp-server 0.5.7\n- mcp 1.29.0 (pinned `<2`; `FastMCP` moved in 2.0 — see #70)\n- Django 6.0.7, Python 3.13","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/issues/71/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gts360/django-mcp-server/issues/71/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]]